<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Charisma</h1>
<p>Charisma (CHA) is one of your abilities. It determines:
</p>
<ul><li><b>Your mana.</b> Your maximum mana grows with your charisma and your brain together (see <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Points</a>).</li>
<li><b>How fast your mana comes back.</b> When your charisma equals your magic or divine power, whichever is higher, mana returns at the normal rate; more charisma makes it faster, less makes it slower.</li>
<li><b>Some skills</b> that work on others: soothing a monster and ventriloquism compare your charisma with your target's.</li>
<li><b>Resisting plague</b>, together with your constitution.</li></ul>
<p>Some aggressive monsters pick whom to attack by charisma among other 
abilities. The spell charisma raises it for a while, and the curse spell 
lowers it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Abilities</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spell Charisma</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Points</a>
</pre>




</div>